post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'

Centaur DE is installed.

  1. Enable the privileged service:
       systemctl enable --now centaur-sysd.service

  2. Log out and pick "Centaur" in your display manager.

  Lock in the topbar power menu uses swaylock with Centaur's lock screen
  (/usr/share/centaur/themes/swaylock.conf). A ~/.config/swaylock/config of
  your own takes precedence.

  Right-clicking the desktop opens Centaur's menu (Terminal, Change
  Background, Display Settings, Lock Screen, Log Out), themed like the rest
  of the desktop. An existing ~/.config/labwc/menu.xml is saved once as
  menu.xml.pre-centaur before Centaur's replaces it.

  Screenshots: Print (whole screen), Shift+Print (area), Super+Shift+S
  (options), or "Take Screenshot…" in the desktop menu. Saved to
  ~/Pictures/Screenshots and copied to the clipboard.

  Wallpaper: "Background" in the launcher (centaur-background). Centaur's
  own wallpapers are in /usr/share/backgrounds/centaur; pictures you add are
  copied to ~/.local/share/backgrounds.

  Display settings: "Displays" in the launcher (centaur-displays). Kept
  layouts are saved per user and restored at login by centaur-settingsd.

  Suspend is hidden in virtual machines, which usually cannot wake from it.
  Override with: gsettings set org.centaur.topbar suspend-button always

  Settings are GSettings keys; list them with:
       gsettings list-recursively | grep org.centaur

  Centaur runs on labwc, its official compositor, installed with this
  package together with Xwayland for X11 applications.

  For the network, battery and volume indicators, the monospace font and the
  alternative icon theme, install the optional dependencies too:
       sudo pacman -S --needed --asdeps networkmanager upower libpulse \
            pipewire-pulse libnotify ttf-jetbrains-mono papirus-icon-theme

  Known gap in 0.1.x: the topbar's workspace pager and focused-window
  indicator need a compositor that reports them. labwc does not yet, so
  those two indicators are absent.

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  systemctl daemon-reload >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
  echo "Restart centaur-sysd to pick up this version:"
  echo "  systemctl restart centaur-sysd.service"
  echo "Reload a running Centaur session (it respawns the topbar at once):"
  echo "  pkill -x centaur-topbar"
}

pre_remove() {
  systemctl disable --now centaur-sysd.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
}
